WonderZoom patch for WindVChen/INR-Harmonization @ 19946ddaffad415ee72fdda7741db8a2b4379606
Apply with: git -C external/INR-Harmonization apply third_party/inr_harmonization/inr_harmonization.patch
(scripts/setup_third_party.sh inr runs 'git apply --check' first and then copies
third_party/inr_harmonization/inr_harmonization_model.py next to the patched sources.)

Changes:
  (a) utils/misc.py is moved to a top-level misc.py and every importer now uses
      'import misc' / 'from misc import ...'. WonderZoom has its own 'utils' package
      on sys.path, so 'from utils.misc import ...' would resolve to the wrong package.
  (b) np.int -> np.int32 in model/hrnetv2/hrnet_ocr.py (np.int was removed in NumPy 1.24).
  (c) model/backbone.py: the HRNet ImageNet initialisation path is read from the
      INR_HRNET_PRETRAINED environment variable and skipped when it is unset. The
      harmonization checkpoint (Resolution_RAW_iHarmony4.pth) contains the full weights,
      so inference does not need it. Upstream used a hard-coded Windows path and called
      exit(1) when the file was missing.
  (d) inference_for_arbitrary_resolution_image.py: POSIX default path for --pretrained.

